# CMS69 BMI Screening — measure caseload

// A clinical scenario where a patient with a high baseline BMI receives
// a weight assessment referral, and a follow-up reading later in the
// measurement period shows improvement. The patient satisfies the CMS69
// Numerator via the High-BMI-and-Follow-Up path.

library "CMS69 BMI Screening".
covers "cms69".


// ============ Patient facts ============

fact "Jane Doe":
- name is "Jane Doe".
- birth date is "1980-01-01".
- defined by "Patient".


// ============ Clinical facts ============

fact "Baseline Wellness Visit":
- code is "http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt|99395".
- date is "2026-01-15".
- defined by "cms69-ExternalPrimitives"."Encounters to Evaluate BMI".

fact "High Baseline BMI":
- code is "http://loinc.org|39156-5".
- date is "2026-01-15".
- value is 32.4.
- defined by "cms69-ExternalPrimitives"."BMI Observations".

fact "Weight Assessment Referral Order":
- code is "http://snomed.info/sct|306163007".
- date is "2026-01-15".
- stage is ordered.
- defined by "cms69-strategy"."Order Weight Assessment Referral".

fact "Follow-up Normal BMI":
- code is "http://loinc.org|39156-5".
- date is "2026-07-15".
- value is 24.1.
- defined by "cms69-ExternalPrimitives"."BMI Observations".


// ============ Cases ============

case "Jane's high BMI is followed up with a weight assessment referral":
- description is `Jane's baseline BMI at her wellness visit is high and she
  receives a weight assessment referral. No overweight/obese diagnosis is
  documented, so the referral is neither justified by nor preceded by a
  qualifying diagnosis — the intervention does not count toward the CMS69
  numerator. Jane is in the denominator but NOT the numerator: a care gap.
  (The CEL fact model cannot yet express a Condition's onset, clinicalStatus,
  or reasonCode (issue #285), so a numerator-satisfying case cannot be
  authored; and the result assertions are not executed locally (issue #70),
  so these are hand-traced language-correct oracles, not execution-proven
  determinations.)`.
- subject is "Jane Doe".
- fact is "Baseline Wellness Visit".
- fact is "High Baseline BMI".
- fact is "Weight Assessment Referral Order".
- fact is "Follow-up Normal BMI".
- result is "Initial Population" is true.
- result is "Denominator Exclusions" is false.
- result is "Numerator" is false.
- result is "Denominator Exceptions" is false.
